# Release workflow

Use when the user asks to prepare a release, bump the extension version, update the changelog for a cut, package a VSIX before publish, or create a version tag.

## Source of truth

1. Follow `.cursor/skills/prepare-release/SKILL.md` step by step.
2. Align git/tag and GitHub Release expectations with `doc/guide/release.md`.

## Files to keep in sync

- Bump **`package.json`** and **`package-lock.json`** (root `version` and `packages[""].version`) to the same target version.
- Add or finalize **`CHANGELOG.md`** (dated `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section; move items out of `[Unreleased]` when cutting).

## After verification

Run the scripts from `package.json` listed in the skill (typically `compile`, `lint`, `test`, `build`, `package` / `package:vsix` when packaging).

Create **`git tag v<version>`** and push only after the maintainer confirms; tag name must match `package.json` with a leading `v`.
